Then in the else branch (line 4574-4598) since `img_n != out_n`:
- The loop at line 4578 processes pixels from x-1 down to 1
- For each pixel: `cur[filter_bytes]=255` sets alpha high byte
- Then at line 4593-4597, the low byte is set for all pixels

But the color components (p[0], p[1]) are set from the raw data through filtering. So they should be initialized from the PNG data.

